OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,! ,$A(W)
OL,3,GNEWSACouncil wins legal fight over
OL,4,Aflags on lamp-posts
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe council's lawyers said the flags
OL,7,Fwere a road safety risk and created
OL,8,Ftensions, but supporters argued an
OL,9,Forder would breach the European
OL,10,FConvention on Human Rights.
OL,12,FJudge Emma Kelly said there was a
OL,13,F"compelling need" to grant the interim
OL,14,Finjunction.
OL,23,APub: 18-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
